From 74abed5170a35e2ab80235e61087ae1ea2b6c2d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:08:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 079/109] fix(classify): count only real crashes, restart an
 omitted model, keep routing off a paused model

- The watchdog stops a backend whose /health stays silent for three probes
  after a request has run its 90 s grace, about 105 s, inside the 120 s
  classify forward. That kill was recorded as backend_crashed_on_input, so
  three slow inputs paused a model that never crashed. It now answers 504
  backend_unresponsive_on_input, is still not retried, and is not counted.
- /v1/classify without "model" looked for the sole classifier among live
  backends only, so after a crash it answered 400 and never restarted the
  model or reported its pause. Dead backends now count, as on the image route.
- Router classifier helpers loaded their model before Router::classify checked
  the crash pause, so a registered router restarted a paused classifier. The
  helper now fails before loading, and the classifier's on_error applies.
- record_classify_crash no longer throws when a backend error's code is not a
  string.

The fake engine gains a hang input that also blocks its /health, and the
suite gains a 12 MiB multipart upload (accepted: httplib parses multipart
into the form and leaves the body empty, so it is not counted twice).

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
